.TH SBX 1 "2026-08-12" "supaswitch 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sbx \- per\-repo Supabase account switching
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sbx add
.I profile
.br
.B sbx list
.br
.B sbx remove
.I profile
.br
.B sbx token
.I profile
.br
.B sbx use
.I profile
.br
.B sbx install
.RI [ directory ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Supabase CLI keeps a single global login, so working in repositories that
belong to different Supabase accounts means re\-running
.B supabase login
on every switch, and two shells cannot use two accounts at the same time.
.PP
.B sbx
stores one personal access token per named
.I profile
in the macOS Keychain, and installs a transparent
.B supabase
shim ahead of the real CLI in
.BR PATH .
On each invocation the shim looks for a
.I .supabase\-account
file, walking up from the current directory, and exports that profile's token
as
.B SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN
before executing the real binary. Because that variable takes precedence over
the CLI's stored login and is set per process, repositories select their
account by location, and sessions in different repositories never interfere.
.PP
Repositories opt in by committing a
.I .supabase\-account
file containing a profile name. The file holds no secret and is safe to commit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B add \fIprofile\fR
Store a Supabase personal access token under
.IR profile .
The token is read from a hidden prompt, or from standard input when not
attached to a terminal, and never appears in the process arguments. Create
tokens at https://supabase.com/dashboard/account/tokens
.TP
.B list
Print the names of all stored profiles.
.TP
.B remove \fIprofile\fR
Delete a profile's token from the Keychain.
.TP
.B token \fIprofile\fR
Print a profile's token on standard output, for feeding other tools. Treat the
output as a secret.
.TP
.B use \fIprofile\fR
Change the
.I global
Supabase login to this profile by running
.BR "supabase login" .
This is the old\-style switch and affects every repository at once; prefer
.I .supabase\-account
files instead.
.TP
.B install \fR[\fIdirectory\fR]
Symlink
.B sbx
and the
.B supabase
shim into
.IR directory ,
defaulting to
.IR ~/.local/bin ,
and install this manual page alongside them. Refuses to replace a file it does
not already own. The directory must precede the real Supabase CLI in
.BR PATH ;
the command warns when it does not.
.SH ACCOUNT RESOLUTION
For each
.B supabase
invocation the shim resolves an account as follows.
.IP 1. 4
If
.B SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN
is already set in the environment it is left untouched; an explicit token
always wins.
.IP 2. 4
Otherwise the nearest
.I .supabase\-account
file, searching upward from the current directory, names the profile whose
token is used. A named profile with no stored token is a fatal error, never a
silent fall\-through to another account.
.IP 3. 4
Otherwise the shim changes nothing and the CLI behaves exactly as it would
without
.BR sbx ,
using the global login.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .supabase\-account
Per\-repository profile selection: one profile name.
.B #
comments and blank lines are ignored. Contains no secret.
.TP
.I ~/.local/bin/supabase
The shim, as installed by
.BR "sbx install" .
.PP
Tokens are held in the macOS Keychain as generic passwords with service
.B sbx
and account name equal to the profile name. They are never written to disk in
plain text.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN
Read, and set for the child process. When already set, the shim defers to it
and performs no lookup.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B sbx
exits 0 on success and 1 on error. When the shim delegates to the real
Supabase CLI, that program's exit status is passed through unchanged.
.SH EXAMPLES
Store a token for each account, then bind two repositories to them:
.PP
.EX
sbx add work
sbx add client\-a
echo work > ~/src/repo\-one/.supabase\-account
echo client\-a > ~/src/repo\-two/.supabase\-account
.EE
.PP
Each repository now uses its own account, including at the same time:
.PP
.EX
cd ~/src/repo\-one && supabase projects list   # as work
cd ~/src/repo\-two && supabase projects list   # as client\-a
.EE
.PP
Override the repository's profile for a single command:
.PP
.EX
SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=sbp_... supabase projects list
.EE
.SH NOTES
A process keeps the
.B PATH
it started with, so shells and coding\-agent sessions started before
.B sbx install
continue to use the real CLI and the global login, silently and without error.
Restart them, and confirm with
.BR "command \-v supabase" ,
which must print the shim's path.
.PP
.B "supabase link"
state is stored per repository, under
.IR supabase/.temp/ ,
and is unaffected by changing accounts. A linked command that fails with an
authorization error after a switch indicates the wrong account, not a broken
link; no re\-link is needed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR supabase (1)
.PP
